{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Breeze feels like a natural next choice after Old Sock because the Clapton connection and relaxed blues sound give me a specific reason to listen now.",
    "Croz, Standing in the Breach, and Cass County fit my interest in thoughtful songs and roots-oriented music, even though I would save them for another time."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Houses of the Holy and Physical Graffiti lean heavier than the relaxed, song-focused music I want right now.",
    "The live collections do not suit this listening session, even when the artist appeals to me, and The Endless River lacks the vocal focus I currently want."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat an interest in familiar rock musicians as a reason to want their heavier records too.",
    "They seem to assume that liking an artist's sound also means wanting a lengthy live collection right now."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection to Old Sock matters most when it carries through to laid-back blues, rather than just another well-known rock artist.",
    "There is a difference between music I might enjoy eventually and something compelling enough to choose today; an unfamiliar roots act is less likely to get me listening without a stronger connection."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in roots music and established songwriters, but miss how much relaxed blues, vocals, and a clear connection matter to my choice today."
}"}
